roles:
OAW LLM wiki (docs/raw -> wiki_sync.py -> docs/knowledge, plus context_hub recall/get) keeps these jobs:
- the only record of project decisions and the reasons behind them;
- the verbatim source text, provenance per source (ref, ID, date), and recall citations as source:line;
- the guard that refuses to overwrite manual pages, and AI annotations that survive rebuilds;
- metadata, link, freshness, orphan and moved-source lint, and the ssot_mirrors cross-check;
- the default recall over docs/knowledge;
- the release gate (test_wiki_sync, the repo-wiki lint) and the --profile knowledge installer.

graphify gets two jobs only. It is an optional external tool the user installs per project and runs by hand, with no LLM backend, no skill, no always-on block and no git hooks. Its output stays in graphify-out/, which is gitignored.
- (1) A structural code map and ranked navigation of the code (graphify query/path/explain over AST nodes). It does not replace recall for decisions.
- (2) A signal linking docs to code: backtick `path::Symbol` mentions in docs/raw become references edges with no LLM, and `graphify affected <Symbol>` answers "which notes cite the code I changed". Nothing from the agent goes back into docs/knowledge; the agent refreshes notes through wiki_sync as usual.

graphify never writes into docs/. `graphify export wiki`, its LLM pass over documents, its memory and reflect loop, and its router rules are not adopted.

